<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Build-configuration driven (see App.xcodeproj): development for
	     Debug, production for the App target's Release. It was hardcoded
	     to "development", which silently delivers ZERO pushes from
	     TestFlight or the App Store — the device registers against the
	     APNs sandbox while FCM sends to production, and nothing anywhere
	     reports an error. APS_ENVIRONMENT is defined at PROJECT level for
	     both configurations too, so this can never expand empty and break
	     signing. Verify the archived app with the codesign command in
	     docs/SHIP-CHECKLIST.md before uploading; the failure is silent
	     otherwise. -->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>$(APS_ENVIRONMENT)</string>
	<!-- Invite links (universal links): iOS verifies this domain against
	     /.well-known/apple-app-site-association at install time. That file
	     carries the real Team ID as of 2026-08-05 (it held a placeholder
	     before, and this comment said so) — so verification now depends on
	     hosting having been redeployed since, plus iOS's own CDN fetch,
	     which is cached and can take a day. Until both, links open the
	     hosted fallback page instead of the app, which still works.

	     This entitlement is why the App ID needs the Associated Domains
	     capability enabled: a provisioning profile cannot grant an
	     entitlement the App ID does not have, so missing it fails the
	     ARCHIVE, not just the links. -->
	<!-- (App ID capabilities registered 2026-08-05: Push Notifications +
	     Associated Domains, and deliberately nothing else — an unused
	     capability is an entitlement to carry and a question to answer.
	     Sign in with Apple joined on 2026-09-07, and it is not an
	     exception to that rule: it is required rather than useful, see
	     below.) -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:prvfire33.web.app</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Sign in with Apple (2026-09-07). NOT a preference: guideline 4.8
	     requires it wherever a third-party login is offered, and the app
	     is gaining an account wall with Google behind it
	     (docs/SIGNIN-PLAN.md §4). Without the wall the app passed 4.8 by
	     requiring no login at all, which is why this was absent until now.

	     THE ORDERING TRAP IS THE SAME ONE THE ASSOCIATED-DOMAINS COMMENT
	     ABOVE RECORDS, and it is why this key landed in its own commit
	     after the code: a provisioning profile cannot grant an entitlement
	     the App ID does not have, so if Sign in with Apple is not ticked
	     on com.cosaxo.insight in the developer portal, this fails the
	     ARCHIVE — a red release run on a tree where nothing else is wrong,
	     and an error that names the entitlement rather than the portal.
	     The dry run (ios-release.yml with upload off) is the cheap proof:
	     it archives, signs and exports without spending a build number.

	     "Default" is the whole value — the array exists because Apple also
	     defines it for the sibling flow where an app signs users in on
	     another app's behalf, which this is not. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
